acceptanceCriteria:
US-002 | The three seed-vs-live files are NOT symlinks and keep main's index mode. This is the fence against the catastrophic failure mode: symlinking `scripts/cam/journal.md` to its seed would destroy the live journal, make the seed the journal, and ship cam-cli history to every downstream project. Species: INVARIANCE PIN, comparand derived from `git ls-tree main`. Oracle:
rc=0
for f in scripts/cam/journal.md scripts/cam/patterns.md scripts/cam/suggestions.jsonl; do
  [ -L "$f" ] && { echo "IS-SYMLINK $f"; rc=1; }
  now=$(git ls-files -s -- "$f" | cut -d' ' -f1); was=$(git ls-tree main -- "$f" | cut -d' ' -f1)
  [ -n "$was" ] || { echo "NO-MAIN-ENTRY $f"; rc=1; continue; }
  [ "$now" = "$was" ] || { echo "MODE-DRIFT $f now=$now main=$was"; rc=1; }
done
exit $rc
Verified GREEN on main 2026-08-11: exit 0. The implementer must red-sweep this in a scratch worktree before trusting it: `ln -sf ../../templates/scripts/cam/journal.md scripts/cam/journal.md && git add -A && <gate>` must exit non-zero.

US-002 | The agents-md gate's scan surface still covers every persona on disk after the personas become symlinks. This is the criterion that catches the Bun.Glob trap; `scripts/validate-agents-md.ts` must pass `followSymlinks: true` (or `onlyFiles: false`) to its scanSync call. Species: INVARIANCE PIN, comparand derived from a live readdirSync. Oracle:
bun -e '
const { resolveScanTargets, SCAN_FILES } = await import("./scripts/validate-agents-md.ts");
const fs = require("node:fs");
const want = SCAN_FILES.length + fs.readdirSync(".claude/agents").filter(f => f.endsWith(".md")).length;
const got  = resolveScanTargets(process.cwd()).length;
if (got !== want) { console.error(`agents-md scan surface ${got} != readdir-derived ${want}`); process.exit(1); }
console.log("ok scan targets =", got);
'
Verified GREEN on main 2026-08-11: exit 0, 7 targets. Measured evidence for the trap: on bun 1.3.13, default scanSync over a directory holding 457 symlinks and 1 regular file returned 1 of 458 entries; with followSymlinks:true it returned 458/458.

US-002 + US-004 | The two new gates EXIST in the live GATES array by name, the test file pins the array, and each gate reddens on a planted violation. The name-presence half is what makes this non-tautological: the previous form only checked that the test pinned whatever GATES already contained, so it stayed green if zero gates were added. Species: CHANGE-DETECTION. Oracle:
bun -e '
const { GATES } = await import("./scripts/check-all.ts");
const src = require("node:fs").readFileSync("test/check-all.test.ts","utf8");
let rc = 0;
for (const n of ["symlink-integrity","overlay-drift"]) if (!GATES.some(g => g.name === n)) { console.error(`missing gate: ${n}`); rc = 1; }
const m = /expect\(GATES\)\.toHaveLength\((\d+)\)/.exec(src);
if (!m) { console.error("no toHaveLength pin in test/check-all.test.ts"); rc = 1; }
else if (Number(m[1]) !== GATES.length) { console.error(`test pins ${m[1]} but GATES has ${GATES.length}`); rc = 1; }
for (let i = 0; i < GATES.length; i++) if (!src.includes(`GATES[${i}]?.name`)) { console.error(`no name assertion for GATES[${i}] (${GATES[i].name})`); rc = 1; }
process.exit(rc);
'
Swept RED on main 2026-08-11: exit 1 (neither gate name exists; main has 16 gates with GATES[0..15]?.name all asserted).
PLANTED-VIOLATION HALF, run in a scratch git worktree so the real tree is never mutated, and REQUIRED as part of this criterion rather than left in prose:
w=$(mktemp -d)/wt && git worktree add -q "$w" HEAD && ( cd "$w" \
  && ln -sf ../../templates/scripts/cam/journal.md scripts/cam/journal.md && git add -A \
  && ! bun scripts/check-all.ts --only symlink-integrity ) ; rc=$?
git worktree remove --force "$w" >/dev/null 2>&1; exit $rc
The seed-vs-live fence must exit non-zero when the journal is linked to its seed. CI parity needs no extra work: the workflow runs `bun run check:all -- --json`, the spine, which picks up every manifest gate automatically.

The committed symlink target is RELATIVE, checked on the stored blob rather than on the resolved path. Species: CHANGE-DETECTION. Oracle (run as an additional pass inside the population loop, after the readlink equality check):
rc=0
git ls-files -s | awk '$1=="120000" {print $4}' | while read -r d; do
  tgt=$(git cat-file blob ":$d")
  case "$tgt" in
    /*) echo "ABSOLUTE-TARGET $d -> $tgt"; rc=1 ;;
  esac
  printf '%s\n' "$tgt" | grep -q '^\.\./' || { echo "NON-RELATIVE-TARGET $d -> $tgt"; rc=1; }
done
[ "$(git ls-files -s | awk '$1=="120000"' | wc -l)" -gt 0 ] || { echo "NO-SYMLINKS-TRACKED: probe proves nothing"; exit 1; }
exit $rc
WHY THIS IS SEPARATE FROM THE readlink CHECK (audit finding F-04): the population oracle compares `readlink -f` on both sides, and `readlink -f` resolves an ABSOLUTE link created by `ln -s "$(pwd)/templates/..."` to exactly the same realpath as the intended relative one. An absolute target therefore greens the story locally AND greens check:all, while every fresh clone and the CI runner check out a dangling link. Only the stored blob distinguishes them. Swept RED on main 2026-08-11: exit 1, NO-SYMLINKS-TRACKED (zero tracked symlinks today).
